description:
In order to work in Ireland a non-EEA National, unless they are exempted, must hold a valid employment permit.  Please review the Eligibility and requirements for an employment permit if you are unsure of your eligibility to apply for this vacancy. <br>  Brotherhood Coffee Limited is looking for a full-time Marketing Analyst to join our team. Responsible for planning and executing the company’s digital marketing strategy across a range of digital channels, ensuring consistency with the company’s brand identity; creating and developing engaging, compelling and shareable content; managing and enhancing the company’s online presence and social media channels; developing strategies to increase website traffic, customer engagement and brand awareness; and implementing digital marketing initiatives to support the growth of the company’s coffee, retail, subscription and event services.
Candidates must have at least 2 years’ relevant experience and knowledge of key areas of marketing, including SEO, social media and content marketing; creativity with an ability to think outside the box.
€42,000 per year, 39 hours per week.
4 Ballinteer Rd, Ballinteer, Dublin 16, D16 V343;
Suite 100, Q House, 76 Furze Road, Sandyford Business Park, D18 V6K0;
16 Newtown Park, Stillorgan Park, Blackrock, Co. Dublin, A94 E049;
